# Context

## Background
.discovery/ was ignored since the prototype days ("regenerated;
not source of truth"). By 2026-09 the dir holds the review trail
for score changes: candidate JSONs, judge dismissal rationales,
apply manifests, and the 2026-09-21 Astra release review.

## Decision
Version the curated artifacts on main; keep only
.discovery/atlas-runs/ ignored. Those raw JSONL run transcripts
are 51 MB and grow ~tens of MB per biweekly sweep, so committing
them would permanently bloat history (removal later needs a
history rewrite). Confirmed with the repo owner on 2026-09-22.

## Gotchas
- atlas-runs transcripts stay local-only; treat them as
  regenerable, not as shared evidence.
- The astra-release-review JSON is also tracked on branch
  discovery/deact-biweekly-pdf-fix (5bae6f6, force-added before
  this change) with identical content, so merges stay clean.

